What is Kubernetes?

"Kubernetes is an open-source container orchestration platform used to automate deployment, scaling, load balancing, self-healing, 
 and management of containerized applications."

What is a Node?

"A Node is a physical or virtual machine in a Kubernetes cluster where Pods are scheduled and executed."

What is a Pod?

"A Pod is the smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes that encapsulates one or more containers sharing the same network and storage."

From where does Kubernetes pull images?
"Kubernetes itself does not pull images. It instructs the Container Runtime (such as containerd) to pull images from a container registry. 
By default, if only an image name like nginx is specified, the image is pulled from Docker Hub (docker.io)."

